    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nLSP hovers reference documentation with `file://<path>#<line>#<col>` and netrw can't open them. `#` are treated like alt buffers.\n\n<img width=\"1441\" height=\"428\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/10987132-6c8d-4949-9f6a-64e793f66a38\" />\n\n```\nE194: No alternate file name to substitute for '#': keepalt edit /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/_meta/api.gen.lua#1060#9\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```vim\n:lsp enable lua_ls\n:lua vim.lsp.buf.hover() \" over an API function\n\" Navigate to \"See:\" reference\n<CR>\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nOpens the file at the specified location.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\ndon't wanna setup LSP in vim\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narch linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty\n\n### Installation\n\npacman",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
